# Reviewed required-suite exceptions for binutils 2.47 built in the LFS chroot
# with the chapter 6 compiler. Format and review rules: README.md in this
# directory.
#
# Basis: The LFS 13.1-systemd binutils page states "One test related to gprofng
#   is known to fail." It does not name the test.
#   https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/view/13.1-systemd/chapter08/binutils.html
#   The LFS editors' reference test log for this book version names it: its
#   only non-pass result is this exact line, with the same six pass counts as
#   the run observed here.
#   https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/lfs/build-logs/13.1/i7-14700K/test-logs/820-binutils-2.47
#   (55539 bytes, sha256 696419ce06c5a849c2724ff7d6c0a04456963ff4eb529fd4900e4b0013f16e78,
#   fetched 2026-11-05).
#   In the observed run exactly one result in the whole suite is not a pass,
#   and it is in gprofng: gprofng.display/gp-gmon.exp builds a small program
#   with "gcc -pg", converts its gmon.out with "gprofng display gmon" (which
#   exits 0) and then requires "+-<Total>", "+-main" and "+-gethrtime" in the
#   "gprofng display text -calltree" output of the converted experiment. The
#   retained gprofng.log records "No calltree for" that conversion. The other
#   gprofng programs' results (mttest, synprog, gp-archive, gp-collect-app_F,
#   setpath_map) pass, and jsynprog is unsupported because no Java is present.
#   Why the converted call tree lacks those nodes in this environment has not
#   been traced; no upstream report naming this test was found on 2026-11-05.
#   The gmon converter is not used by any TUP build or runtime step.
# Observed: rehearsal attempt 03 on 2026-11-05, an isolated continuation of
#   failed core run 001 with this page's recipe unchanged, four test jobs:
#   5966 expected passes in six summaries (ld 3304, gas 2098, binutils 351,
#   libsframe 168, libctf 40, gprofng 5), 1 unexpected failure, 59 expected
#   failures, 46 unsupported, 7 untested, no XPASS, UNRESOLVED or ERROR.
@min-pass 5900
FAIL: tmpdir/gp-gmon
